(The First Light) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 688 Tm
(Wake, if you can, before the world insists. The early hour) Tj T*
(belongs to no one, which is precisely why it can belong to you.) Tj T*
(The light at this time is thin and silver and forgiving; it does) Tj T*
(not yet ask anything. Let the kettle do its slow work and stand) Tj T*
(at the window doing nothing in particular.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 587.5 Tm
(A quiet morning is not an empty morning. It is full to the brim) Tj T*
(with small attentions: the cooling of the tea, the particular) Tj T*
(grey of the sky, the sound of a single early bird testing the) Tj T*
(silence. To notice these is not idleness. It is a kind of) Tj T*
(devotion, and the day repays it.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 487 Tm
(Bring a book to the table, but do not hurry to open it. Let the) Tj T*
(morning and the page meet on their own terms. Reading, at this) Tj T*
(hour, is less an activity than a continuation of the quiet by) Tj T*
(other means.) Tj T*
ET

endstream
