1 0 0 1 84 722 Tm
(On Doing Less) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 688 Tm
(The temptation of every morning is to spend it before it has) Tj T*
(begun, to load the hours with errands until they sag. Resist,) Tj T*
(gently. A morning kept half-empty is a vessel that the day may) Tj T*
(pour itself into. The most useful thing you do before nine) Tj T*
(oclock may be to read three pages slowly and forget to check) Tj T*
(the time.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 569 Tm
(There is a mathematics to this that the busy will not believe:) Tj T*
(that less, attended to fully, amounts to more. The page read) Tj T*
(twice is worth four read once. The walk taken without a) Tj T*
(destination returns you somewhere you needed to be.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 487 Tm
(Keep your mornings as you would keep a good book: with a ribbon) Tj T*
(to mark your place, and no great hurry to reach the end.) Tj T*
ET

endstream
