1 0 0 1 84 722 Tm
(A Short Catalogue of Small Joys) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 689 Tm
(The first sip, taken too soon, slightly too hot. The weight of a) Tj T*
(blanket. A letter from someone who still writes letters. The) Tj T*
(particular satisfaction of a sentence that says exactly what it) Tj T*
(means and then stops.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 607 Tm
(The smell of rain not yet fallen. A cats decision to sit upon) Tj T*
(the very book you are reading. The discovery, on the second) Tj T*
(reading, of a line you had somehow walked past the first time,) Tj T*
(as one walks past a door in a familiar house and only later) Tj T*
(wonders what was behind it.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 506.5 Tm
(These are not the great joys, and that is the point. The great) Tj T*
(joys are rare and exhausting. The small ones are inexhaustible,) Tj T*
(and a quiet morning is the net in which they are most easily) Tj T*
(caught.) Tj T*
1 0 0 1 84 400.5 Tm
/F3 12 Tf
18 TL
1 0 0 1 84 400.5 Tm
( End of the Notes ) Tj T*
